@startuml seq-human-turn
title Human Player Turn (Two-Phase Flow, PvP)

actor "Active Player\n(P1)" as P1
actor "Opponent Player\n(P2)" as P2
participant "P1's Browser\n(React SPA)" as SPA1
participant "P2's Browser\n(React SPA)" as SPA2
participant "Flask API\nMatch Blueprint" as API
participant "MatchService" as MS
participant "TurnEngine" as TE
participant "MatchRepository" as MR
database "SQLite" as DB

note over P1, DB
  Precondition: it is P1's turn; match status = ACTIVE, phase = PLAY.
  P1 has already seen their hand and mana. P2 is waiting and polling.
end note

== Phase 2: Card Play (P1 plays one card) ==

P1 -> SPA1 : Click card to play
SPA1 -> API : POST /matches/{id}/cards\n{card_index: N}\nAuthorization: Bearer <jwt>
API -> API : Verify JWT → player_id (P1)
API -> MS : play_card(match_id, player_id, card_index)
MS -> MR : load(match_id)
MR -> DB : SELECT FROM matches WHERE id = ?
DB --> MR : row (JSON)
MR --> MS : Match aggregate
MS -> MS : Verify phase = PLAY\nand active player = P1
MS -> TE : play_card(match, card)
note right of TE
  1. Verify mana >= card cost
  2. Deduct mana
  3. Damage = mana_cost
     (0-cost → Dud, no damage)
  4. Raise CardPlayed, PlayerDamaged
  5. Check win condition:
     if P2 health <= 0 →
     raise GameWon,
     set status = FINISHED
end note
TE --> MS : updated Match
MS -> MR : save(match)
MR -> DB : UPDATE matches SET state = ?
DB --> MR : ok
MS --> API : match state
API --> SPA1 : 200 OK {match_state}
SPA1 --> P1 : Update opponent health,\nremaining mana

== End of P1's Turn / Start of P2's Turn ==

P1 -> SPA1 : Click "End Turn"
SPA1 -> API : POST /matches/{id}/end-turn\nAuthorization: Bearer <jwt>
API -> API : Verify JWT → player_id (P1)
API -> MS : end_turn(match_id, player_id)
MS -> MR : load(match_id)
MR -> DB : SELECT FROM matches WHERE id = ?
DB --> MR : row (JSON)
MR --> MS : Match aggregate
MS -> MS : Verify active player = P1
MS -> TE : end_turn(match)
note right of TE
  Emit TurnEnded for P1
  Advance active player → P2
end note
TE --> MS : updated Match (active = P2)

MS -> TE : begin_turn(match)
note right of TE
  P2's start-of-turn:
  1. Gain mana slot (max 10)
  2. Refill mana
  3. Draw card:
     - Empty deck → BleedingOut (P2 -1 HP)
       then check win condition:
       if P2 health <= 0 →
       raise GameWon,
       set status = FINISHED
     - Hand full (5) → CardDiscarded
  If not finished: set phase = PLAY
end note
TE --> MS : updated Match (P2 phase = PLAY\nor status = FINISHED)
MS -> MR : save(match)
MR -> DB : UPDATE matches SET state = ?
DB --> MR : ok
MS --> API : match state
API --> SPA1 : 200 OK {match_state}
SPA1 --> P1 : Show "Waiting for opponent"\n(or game over if FINISHED)

== P2 discovers it is their turn (polling) ==

SPA2 -> API : GET /matches/{id}\nAuthorization: Bearer <jwt>
API -> MS : get_match(match_id, player_id)
MS -> MR : load(match_id)
MR -> DB : SELECT FROM matches WHERE id = ?
DB --> MR : row (JSON)
MR --> MS : Match aggregate
MS -> MS : Verify player_id is a\nparticipant; omit opponent's hand
MS --> API : match state (opponent hand hidden)
API --> SPA2 : 200 OK {match_state\n active_player = P2}
SPA2 --> P2 : Show P2's new hand,\nmana, and health

@enduml
